{
  "comment": "Agent Emailing 0.4.0 conformance cases (SPEC.md §12). Every envelope is a frame of Agent Messaging wire version 0.4.0, carrying A2A objects as A2A over Agent Messaging says, except the 0.3.0 envelope of case e33, which a receiver still accepts in the window of SPEC.md §3.2. A knock and its answer are channel requests and carry no payload.a2a (A2A over Agent Messaging §11). Each case names a fixture, the receiving role, the identity it receives as, the time to judge freshness by, and the expected outcome. Cases are independent: each starts with an empty duplicate memory, and a case with `after` first replays the case it names. Inputs a case may give: `carrier_auth`, the receiving carrier's SPF, DKIM and DMARC results; `admission`, the stance the receiver's door takes toward the sender (`allow` when absent); `standing`, how the sender's standing came out (a vouch and a verified name card when absent); `memory_bound`, the duplicate memory's bound; and `sent`, the sending agent's own records of the emails it sent. Cases e20 to e32 came with Agent Emailing 0.3.0, and e33 and e34 with 0.4.0. `person_view` is what software that shows the human part to a person must conclude (SPEC.md §3.3). THE FIXTURES ARE THE AUTHORITY: when an implementation disagrees with them, the implementation changes.",
